592186045417] [17592186050452 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054788 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050452 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050452 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054790 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050452 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054791 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050452 #edb/ref 1031 "Collecting Like Terms in Linear Expressions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050452 #edb/ref 1033 134 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050452 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "4a33a1d4-8dfa-5e25-8ed4-4aa1496ac8a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050496 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048138 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050496 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048919 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050496 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050496 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050496 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050496 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050496 #edb/ref 1031 "Simplifying Square Root Expressions Using the Product Rule" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050496 #edb/ref 1033 389 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050496 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "4dc7f0d4-7695-5efd-99c0-299924cc9d4b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179463 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1373" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179463 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $9\\sqrt{p - 4} - 7\\sqrt{p - 4} .$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179463 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "13f8fdac-32c2-5f2a-a818-cde14e59299e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179463 #edb/ref 1074 "We can combine the two $\\sqrt{p - 4}$ terms together, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9\\sqrt{p-4}-7\\sqrt{p-4} & = \\\\ (9-7)\\sqrt{p-4} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{p-4} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179464 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1374" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179464 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $\\sqrt{12x}-\\sqrt{27x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179464 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "eb35e7da-e6d0-5811-a2ee-92390f71c5f7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179464 #edb/ref 1074 "We simplify each of the radical terms using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{12x}-\\sqrt{27x} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4\\cdot 3x}-\\sqrt{9\\cdot 3x} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{3x}-\\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{3x} & = \\\\ 2\\cdot \\sqrt{3x}-3\\cdot \\sqrt{3x} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{3x}-3\\sqrt{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we combine like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3x}-3\\sqrt{3x} & = \\\\ (2-3)\\cdot \\sqrt{3x} & = \\\\ (-1)\\cdot \\sqrt{3x} & = \\\\ -\\sqrt{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179619 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9723" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179619 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $10\\sqrt[3]{y} + 2\\sqrt[3]{y} - 7\\sqrt{y}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179619 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "213ad0ee-813b-5a4b-8926-5fbd1aed4906" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179619 #edb/ref 1074 "We can combine the two $\\sqrt[3]{y}$ terms together, but we cannot combine the $\\sqrt[3]{y}$ and $\\sqrt{y}$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t10\\sqrt[3]{y} + 2\\sqrt[3]{y} - 7\\sqrt{y} &= \\[5pt]\n\t\t(10 + 2)\\sqrt[3]{y} - 7\\sqrt{y} &= \\[5pt]\n\t\t12\\sqrt[3]{y}-7\\sqrt{y} &\n\t}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179751 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180162 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186501140 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186501154 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186501180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186501203 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186502098 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186502138 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759